.TH PAUSE 2
.SH NAME
pause \- stop until signal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "pause( )"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pause
never returns normally.
It is used to give up control while waiting
for a signal from
.BR kill (2)
or
.BR alarm (2).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
kill(1), kill(2), alarm(2), signal(2), setjmp(3)
.SH ASSEMBLER
(pause = 29.)
.TP
PDP-11:
.nf
sys pause
.fi
.TP
8086:
.nf
BX = 29
int 0Xf1
.fi
.sp
